Consider this mutable C# struct and method:

```csharp
struct Counter
{
    public int Value;

    public void Increment()
    {
        Value++;
    }
}

static void Advance(in Counter counter)
{
    counter.Increment();
}
```

The caller runs:

```csharp
Counter counter = new Counter { Value = 4 };
Advance(in counter);
```

What is the caller's `counter.Value` afterward? Explain how the `in` parameter affects the call to `Increment()`.
